<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Incident at the Gaoping Tombs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">249</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The incident at the Gaoping Tombs was the coup of 249 in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-yi">Sima Yi</a> seized control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> state. While the regent Cao Shuang escorted the young emperor Cao Fang to the imperial tombs at Gaoping outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, Sima Yi took the capital. Cao Shuang surrendered and was executed with his allies, and the Sima family ruled Wei until founding the Jin dynasty in 266.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/incident-at-the-gaoping-tombs.jpg" alt="Incident at the Gaoping Tombs" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 冯墨农 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%8F%B8%E9%A9%AC%E6%87%BF%E8%AF%88%E7%97%85%E8%B5%9A%E6%9B%B9%E7%88%BD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
